,"scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Emmitt Finnie faceoff won against Juraj Slafkovský","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:16"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"5"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5188599","displayName":"Emmitt Finnie","shortName":"E. Finnie"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4915349","displayName":"Juraj Slafkovsky","shortName":"J. Slafkovsky"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1831","fullName":"Bell Centre","address":{"city":"Montreal","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1831.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":20962,"officials":[{"fullName":"Chris Rooney","displayName":"Chris Rooney","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Garrett Rank","displayName":"Garrett Rank","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Bevan Mills","displayName":"Bevan Mills","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Ryan Jackson","displayName":"Ryan Jackson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Bolduc scores in shootout as the Canadiens outlast the Red Wings 1-0","description":"— Zachary Bolduc scored in the sixth round of a shootout, Jacob Fowler made 30 saves and the Montreal Canadiens beat the Detroit Red Wings 1-0 on Saturday night.","story":"MONTREAL -- — Zachary Bolduc scored in the sixth round of a shootout, Jacob Fowler made 30 saves and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/mtl/montreal-canadiens\">Montreal Canadiens</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/det/detroit-red-wings\">Detroit Red Wings</a> 1-0 on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              After Bolduc beat <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587994/daniil-tarasov\">Daniil Tarasov</a> through the pads for the first score in the tiebreaker, Fowler stopped <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149175/nate-danielson\">Nate Danielson</a>.\n\n\r\n              Montreal ended a three-game losing streak to improve to 2-2-1. It won for first time on home ice in three outings this season.\n\n\r\n              Fowler had his second career shutout for the Canadiens. The 21-year-old was making his second straight start for Montreal after being recalled from the Laval Rocket of the American Hockey League on Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              Tarasov made 30 saves in his first start for the Red Wings.\n\n\r\n              Detroit (1-3-1), playing in its first road game of the season, dropped its second game in two nights after falling 6-3 to the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sea/seattle-kraken\">Seattle Kraken</a> on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              Cole Caufield’s shot 1:16 into the game was deemed not to have crossed the goal line, while Bolduc’s second-period goal was disallowed due to goaltender interference by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4393049/jake-evans\">Jake Evans</a> on Tarasov. A third apparent Montreal goal, this one courtesy of <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233880/alexandre-texier\">Alexandre Texier</a>, was called back for offside midway through overtime.\n\n\r\n              In addition to cheering on the home team, Canadiens fans spent much of the game showing their appreciation for Red Wings forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114755/dylan-larkin\">Dylan Larkin</a>. The crowd repeatedly broke into chants of “We want Larkin! We want Larkin!” in a bid to persuade the American to make Montreal his next destination. The former Red Wings captain requested a trade out of Detroit this past offseason.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Red Wings: Host New Jersey on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Canadiens: Host Buffalo on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-11T02:41:26Z"}}